          </table>
        </div>

        <h3>Letting viewers steer the wheel directly</h3>
        <p>
          A stronger variation: let donors vote in real time on which segment
          gets added or removed. A donation adds the outcome someone most wants
          to see, or removes the one they'd rather skip. The wheel becomes a
          live document shaped by the audience, and it tends to spike chat
          activity every time it visibly changes — which keeps new viewers
          engaged and gives them a reason to donate too.
        </p>

        <div class="box box-success">
          <div class="box-label">✅ Charity stream wheel checklist</div>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Keep the current total and next milestone visible on screen
              throughout
            </li>
            <li>
              Announce each outcome before and after completing it, for viewers
              who just joined
            </li>
            <li>
              Execute every earned spin right away — banking spins deflates the
              momentum the donation created
            </li>
            <li>
              Hold one big outcome back for the final milestone and tell the
              audience it exists from the start
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- ═══ SECTION 6 ═══ -->
        <h2 id="audience-participation">
          6. Letting the Audience Co-Author the Wheel
        </h2>
        <div class="platform-badge badge-both">🎮 Twitch + YouTube Live</div>

        <p>
          These formats hand part of the wheel over to the audience — through
          submissions, votes, or names placed directly on it. That shift turns
          the stream from something performed at viewers into something built
          with them.
        </p>

        <div class="idea-grid">
          <div class="idea-card twitch">
            <div class="idea-emoji">💬</div>
            <div class="idea-num">Format 01 · Chat Integration</div>
            <h3>Live Chat Controls the Segments</h3>
            <p>
              Run a 60-second vote, add the winning suggestion to the wheel on
              camera, then spin. The audience watches the wheel get built in
              real time — a mod helps filter suggestions so it stays manageable.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="idea-card youtube">
            <div class="idea-emoji">👥</div>
            <div class="idea-num">Format 02 · Viewer Name Wheel</div>
            <h3>Spin to Pick a Viewer's Challenge</h3>
            <p>
              Subscribers submit a dare and their username together; both land
              on the wheel. The spin picks the dare and its author at once —
              public credit that pushes people to submit something worth landing
              on.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="idea-card teal">
            <div class="idea-emoji">🗳️</div>
            <div class="idea-num">Format 03 · Pre-Stream Voting</div>
            <h3>The Audience Builds the Wheel in Advance</h3>
            <p>
              Post a poll a day ahead letting followers pick 8–10 segments for
              the next stream's wheel. It creates pre-stream buzz and guarantees
              the wheel actually reflects what your audience wants to watch.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="idea-card orange">
            <div class="idea-emoji">🎰</div>
            <div class="idea-num">Format 04 · Channel Points Wheel</div>
            <h3>Viewers Spend Points to Influence Spins</h3>
            <p>
              Let points trigger a spin, add a temporary segment, weight an
              outcome, or remove one entirely. It builds a small economy around
              the wheel and turns point-spending into a direct signal of what
              viewers value.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="idea-card">
            <div class="idea-emoji">🏅</div>
            <div class="idea-num">Format 05 · Subscriber Tournament</div>
            <h3>Subscribers Compete via the Wheel</h3>
            <p>
              Load subscriber names and spin to pick who faces off each round —
              trivia, a quick game, whatever chat decides. Eliminated names come
              off the wheel. Scales cleanly from 8 to 64 entrants.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="idea-card gold">
            <div class="idea-emoji">🎁</div>
            <div class="idea-num">Format 06 · Prize Giveaway Wheel</div>
            <h3>Spin to Select the Winner</h3>
            <p>
              Load every qualifying entry and spin live — seeing all entries
